# OCR caches, not results. `pagetext/` is the per-page text of every PDF and
# `parts/` and `raw/` are per-file intermediates — together several megabytes of
# machine output that any of the extractors will regenerate. The JSON beside
# them is the result and is tracked, because a batch that cites a page number
# should be checkable against what the page actually said.
pagetext/
parts/
raw/
__pycache__/
status-*.json

# Rendered pages. The answer-key recovery rasterises every page of every
# end-of-module paper to find highlights that exist only as pixels; the images
# are a cache, regenerable from the PDFs, and megabytes of them.
*.png
*.ppm
*.jpg
